You can create any .txt file in the root directory and add
multiple app base URLs to it, with one URL per line.

Example:

https://your-app.koyeb.app
https://your-app.onrender.com
https://yourdomain.com

The application automatically reads all .txt files in the root
directory and pings every valid URL starting with http:// or https://.

If you don't want to create a .txt file, you can directly add
your app base URL(s) to the ENDPOINTS list in alive.py.

Both methods are supported, and URLs from both sources will be
ping together.
